{"name":"Still Life in Grey","hex":"#a1a39f","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"still","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Not moving; calm.","Not effervescing; not sparkling."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Without motion.","Up to a time, as in the preceding time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/still"},{"term":"life","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The state of organisms preceding their death, characterized by biological processes such as metabolism and reproduction and distinguishing them from inanimate objects; the state of being alive and living.","The status possessed by any of a number of entities, including animals, plants, fungi, bacteria, and sometimes viruses, which have the properties of replication and metabolism."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To replace components whose operational lifetime has expired."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/life"},{"term":"grey","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray.","Synonym of coloured (pertaining to the mixed race of black and white)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Commonwealth standard spelling of gray."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/grey"}],"entries":[{"title":"Still life","blocks":[{"text":"A still life is a work of art depicting mostly inanimate subject matter, typically commonplace objects which are either natural or human-made."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Juan_S%C3%A1nchez_Cot%C3%A1n_-_Still_Life_with_Game%2C_Vegetables_and_Fruit%2C_1602.jpg/330px-Juan_S%C3%A1nchez_Cot%C3%A1n_-_Still_Life_with_Game%2C_Vegetables_and_Fruit%2C_1602.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Still_life"},{"title":"Still","blocks":[{"text":"A still is an apparatus used to distill liquid mixtures by heating to selectively boil and then cooling to condense the vapor. A still uses the same concepts as a basic distillation apparatus, but on a much larger scale. Stills have been used to produce perfume and medicine, water for injection (WFI) for pharmaceutical use, generally to separate and purify different chemicals, and to produce distilled beverages containing ethanol."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Glenfiddich_Distillery_stills.jpg/330px-Glenfiddich_Distillery_stills.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Still"},{"title":"Life","blocks":[{"text":"Life is the capacity in matter, formed of one or more units called cells, for processes such as cell signalling, homeostasis, metabolism, cell growth, adaptation, response to stimuli, and reproduction. All life eventually reaches a state of death. Many philosophical definitions of living systems have been proposed, such as self-organising systems. Defining life is further complicated by viruses, which replicate only in host cells, and the possibility of extraterrestrial life, which could be very different from life on Earth. Life exists all over the Earth in air, water, and soil, with many ecosystems forming the biosphere. Some of these are harsh environments occupied only by extremophiles. The life in a particular ecosystem is called its biota."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg/330px-Coral_reef..._South_end_of_my_area_%2814119221571%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Life"},{"title":"Grey","blocks":[{"text":"Grey or gray is an intermediate color between black and white. It is a neutral or achromatic color, meaning that it has no chroma. It is the color of a rain or storm cloud, of ash, and of lead."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg/330px-Loxodonta_africana_by_Ron_Cogswell.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grey"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Still_life_Tor_Marancia_Vatican.jpg/500px-Still_life_Tor_Marancia_Vatican.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Still_life_Tor_Marancia_Vatican.jpg/1280px-Still_life_Tor_Marancia_Vatican.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f2/Still_life_Tor_Marancia_Vatican.jpg/500px-Still_life_Tor_Marancia_Vatican.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Still life on a 2nd-century mosaic, with fish, poultry, dates and vegetables from the Vatican museum","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStill_life_Tor_Marancia_Vatican.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Pompejanischer_Maler_um_70_001.jpg/500px-Pompejanischer_Maler_um_70_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Pompejanischer_Maler_um_70_001.jpg/1280px-Pompejanischer_Maler_um_70_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/ac/Pompejanischer_Maler_um_70_001.jpg/500px-Pompejanischer_Maler_um_70_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Glass bowl of fruit and vases. Roman wall painting in Pompeii (around 70 AD), Naples National Archaeological Museum, Naples, Italy","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APompejanischer_Maler_um_70_001.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9c/Memling%2C_Hans_%E2%80%94_Flowers_in_a_Jug_%28reverse%29.jpg/500px-Mem